---
description: Ratchet method length, nesting depth, and parameter count in touched code
globs: packages/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: true
---

# Method Readability

- When touching a method longer than ~40 lines, do not add more logic inline. Extract named private methods or pure helpers so the top-level method reads as orchestration of clear steps.
- When touching a block nested deeper than 2 levels (e.g. `for > if > for`), extract the inner body into a named helper with intent-revealing name.
- When a function or method exceeds 4 positional parameters, group related parameters into a typed object. Do not keep adding optional trailing arguments.
- Prefer many short methods with clear names assembled in a top-level orchestrator over one long method with section comments.
- These thresholds are ratchets: existing violations are context, not permission to add more.
